    51	There is no linter config; `tests/` (pytest, 171 tests, ~3 min, `python -m pytest tests -q` in the xRIR env) covers the exp_03 tools (`tools/yaw_rotation.py`, `tools/reference_manifest.py`, `tools/paired_stats.py`, `tools/per_sample_metrics.py`, `eval_yaw_rotation.py`, `tools/summarize_yaw.py`). The original eval scripts run `batch_size=1` with `shuffle=True` over the whole test split and print running averages; use `eval_xRIR_backbone.py` (deterministic order, `--max-samples`, JSON summary, identical metric code) for anything that needs to be compared or bounded. Full-split eval takes about an hour per split at ~1.7 samples/s; training is ~1.4 s/iter at batch 32 with TF32 (~3.6 h/epoch on 296k samples), so budget accordingly and rely on `best.pth` / `last.pth` + `--resume`.
    52	
    53	## Architecture
    54	
    55	**Data flow** (`treble_multi_room_dataset/treble_xRIR_dataset.py`). `xRIR_Dataset.__getitem__` returns
    56	`(listener_pos[=0], src_local[3], depth_coord[3,256,512], tgt_wav[1,9600], ref_irs[K,9600], ref_src_local[K,3])`.
    57	- Everything is in the **query receiver's camera frame**. Rotation is fixed to 0, so `get_3d_point_camera_coord` is plain world-frame subtraction. `convert_equirect_to_camera_coord` turns the equirect depth panorama into per-pixel XYZ.
    58	- References are the *other sources* recorded at the **same receiver** (`get_ir_and_location_for_other_sources`), drawn with `np.random.choice` on every call, so batches are non-deterministic. Each reference source is expressed relative to *its own* receiver, which in the baseline equals the query receiver.
    59	- Unseen split = rooms listed in `TEST_ROOMS`; seen split = file list pickled in `seen_test_split.pkl`. `treble_xRIR_seen_dataset.py` is a near-copy of the unseen module with only the split logic changed.
    60	- File naming: `S00{src}_R00{rec}_hybrid_IR.wav` under `<category>/<room>/`; metadata `S00{src}_R00{rec}.json` with `src_loc`/`rec_loc`; depth map `depth_map/<category>/<room>/<rec>.npy`.
    61	
    62	**Model** (`model/xRIR.py`), `xRIR.forward(depth_coord, ref_irs, src_loc, ref_ir_locs, tgt_wav)`:
    63	1. `shift_and_align` time-shifts and rescales each reference RIR by the direct-path distance difference (22050 Hz and 343 m/s hard-coded).
    64	2. One shared `SimpleViT` (`model/simple_vit.py`) runs 2+K times per sample on `(src_loc - depth_coord)/5`, `(-depth_coord)/5`, and `(ref_loc_i - depth_coord)/5`. It returns all patch tokens; `lin_proj_0` is a learned linear pool **over the patch axis** (256 → 1), which only works because the patch count `(256/16)*(512/32)` equals `intermediate_ch=256`. Changing image or patch size silently breaks it.
    65	3. Geometry vectors also go through the sinusoidal `embedding_module_log` (21 channels per scalar → 63 → 256).
    66	4. `AudioEnc` (ResNet-18 on a log-magnitude STFT) encodes each reference. Reference tokens are `lin_proj_2` over `[recv, ref_geo, ref_src, audio]` (5×256 in); the query token is `lin_proj_1` over `[src, recv, source]` (3×256 in).
    67	5. Softmax attention over references followed by a time-conditioned weighting yields the output as a **weighted sum of the reference log-spectrograms**. The model never synthesizes a spectrogram from scratch.
    68	
    69	Output is `[B, 63, 310, 1]` log-magnitude; the returned `tgt_spec` is `[B, 1, 63, 310]` linear magnitude, and callers permute one to match the other.
    70	
    71	**CylindricalViT variant** (`model/cylindrical_vit.py`, `model/xRIR_cyl.py`). `xRIR_Cyl` subclasses `xRIR` and replaces only `source_network` with `CylindricalViT` (per-column gauge alignment `Rz(-theta_c)` of the xyz panorama, elevation-only positional encoding, circular relative-position attention bias). Same dim/depth/heads/mlp_dim and the same `[B, 256, 512]` token output, so everything downstream is shared and a result difference isolates the geometry encoder. `build_xrir(backbone, num_shot)` is the factory used by both backbone scripts. `cylindrical_vit.py` uses PEP 604/585 type hints and needs its `from __future__ import annotations` line to import on Python 3.8.
    72	
    73	**Loss** (`utils/spec_utils.py`): `stft_l1_loss` (L1 in log-magnitude space) + `compute_spect_energy_decay_losses` (Schroeder decay-curve L1). The module is a large grab-bag ported from another project; only those two plus `stft` are used.
    74	
    75	**Eval** (`eval_unseen.py`): `Evaluator` implements EDT / C50 / T60 on waveforms. The predicted magnitude is inverted with `torchaudio` Griffin-Lim and metrics use the first 8000 samples. `eval_seen.py` is a copy that differs only in dataset import and checkpoint loading; keep the two in sync.
    76	
    77	**Sim-to-real** (`sim_to_real/`): two-stage fine-tuning on Hearing-Anything-Anywhere (HAA) rooms. The original scripts (`finetune_all_rooms.py`, `finetune_classroom.py`, `eval_classroom.py`, `haa_*_dataset.py`) carry `/pscratch/...` placeholders and select checkpoints on the test split; keep them as reference only. The runnable pipeline is the parallel set: `prepare_haa.py` (builds `~/data_cache/HAA_xrir/<room>/` from `/media/diskstation/yixunhu/HAA_processed`, normalizing each room by the max amplitude of its 12 DiffRIR training RIRs), `haa_dataset.py` (same tuple as `xRIR_Dataset`; speaker = model "receiver", mics = "sources"; deterministic eval references via `eval_seed`), `finetune_haa.py` (repo recipe, `--backbone`, selection on the DiffRIR validation split), `eval_haa.py` (Table-2 metrics on full 9600-sample waveforms, T60 skipped for `dampened_room`, per-sample JSON), `run_haa_pipeline.sh` (one GPU queue of `<init>:<seed>` jobs into `ckpt/sim2real/`), `summarize_haa.py`. Known asset bugs: the released `sim_to_real/depth_map/complex_room.npy` is byte-identical to `hallway.npy`, and `dampened_room.npy` is misaligned with the pose frame, so the cache uses the HAA_processed renders for those two rooms (`depth_default` in each `meta.json`; `--depth-variant repo` reproduces the released assets). Result (exp_02, 2026-09-06, canonical `ckpt/sim2real/stats.json`): after fine-tuning, the SimpleViT control beats CylindricalViT on 6/11 room×metric cells (hallway by 43–81 %) and loses none; the released checkpoint does not reproduce Table 2 on hallway/complex under this protocol while our control does on EDT. `summarize_haa.py` enforces a strict completeness gate (exact DiffRIR indices, protocol meta, stage `args.json` seed/init/depth_variant) and writes hash-bound `--json`/`--summary` artefacts that the results page consumes.
    78	
    79	## Constants kept in lockstep
    80	
    81	Change these everywhere at once or shapes stop lining up:
    82	- Sample rate 22050 (dataset asserts, `shift_and_align`, every `Evaluator` default) and `max_len=9600`.
    83	- STFT `fft_size=124, hop_size=31, win_length=62` in `xRIR.convert_ir_to_spec` and the `griffin_lim` defined in `eval_*.py` → 63 freq bins × 310 frames (`n_bins=310`). `utils/spec_utils.griffin_lim` has different defaults and is not the one eval uses.
    84	- Depth panorama `(256, 512)` with ViT `patch_size=(16, 32)`; coord scale `5.0` before every ViT input and sinusoidal embedding.
    85	- Sinusoidal embedding `num_freqs=10, max_freq=7` → 21 channels per scalar; `intermediate_ch=256`.
