    20	Estimand basis (adopting FLAC directive 04): every reported cell is the mean ± sample SD over **five evaluation seeds s ∈ {42, 43, 44, 45, 46}**; seed s selects the K-specific reference manifest (`build_manifest(seed=s, num_shot=K)`) and the Griffin-Lim phase seed (`--gl-seed s`). Control and treatment are evaluated under every seed with the same evaluator closure, so every comparison is paired per query and per seed. Inference: per query, the five per-seed errors of each arm are averaged with plain arithmetic means (never `nanmean`; a query with any non-finite value in a cell's mask is excluded from that cell); the paired per-query differences (or ratios inside the resample) are bootstrapped over queries (20 000 resamples, bootstrap seed 0; query-level, this fixed split) with the room-cluster bootstrap (17 rooms) as the secondary interval. **Convergence gate:** every decision-driving query-level bound is recomputed with bootstrap seed 1 on the companion interval whose upper endpoint *is* the decision bound — H1 [Q_0.025, Q_0.975], H2 [Q_0.00625, Q_0.99375], TOST [Q_{0.05/14}, Q_{1−0.05/14}] — and the maximum endpoint movement divided by the seed-0 width must be ≤ 0.10; otherwise no canonical artefact is written until `n_boot` is raised and the gate passes. Single-seed runs are technical diagnostics only and never enter a table or a verdict. H1, H2 and the TOST block are separate family-local claims; there is no omnibus success rule.
