172:- **A1 (2026-09-15, Planner)** — Launch-critical path. The confirmatory pretraining (arm C) depends only on rounds 1 and 2a (encoder, factory, heading tool, trainer entry point, finalizer, launcher, smoke runner) plus the ladder; rounds 2b (evaluation/HAA entry points) and 3 (probe, statistics, producers) are consumed only after pretraining ends (≈ Sep 17 evening). Therefore two integrative reviews replace the single `full` review: `full_train` over rounds 1 + 2a before the pretraining launch (and before the first merge into `main`), and `full` over the whole diff before the first evaluation/HAA launch. Rounds 2b/3 may merge in a later peer window. Motivation: three Codex close reviews on round 2a's finalizer have consumed the night; the GPU-1 hand-over (≈ Sep 16 13:00) must not slip.
175:## 11. Cost, schedule, risks, decisions
177:**GPU cost (expected runtime; reservation ceilings in brackets).** Pretraining 31.2 h [36 h]. Fit/timing probe 10 min. G1 10 min. HAA: 9 fine-tuning jobs (C, D, F × 3 seeds) × ≈ 50 min + zero-shots ≈ 8 h [10 h]; S1 sensitivity ≈ 1 h. Sim: 5 × ≈ 8 min for C ≈ 40 min (exp_04's matching control evaluations took 8.0–8.1 min per seed) [1.5 h]; B fallback ≈ 40 min [1.5 h]. Total ≈ 42 GPU-hours expected [≈ 50 h reserved].
179:**Schedule (agreed with the peer session `xrir-code-25` on 2026-09-14 20:30; contingent on actual hand-over).** GPU 1 frees ≈ Sep 16 13:00 (after exp_05 L_cylindrical and its evaluations; the peer messages when) → fit probe → pretraining Sep 16 ≈ 13:30 → Sep 17 ≈ 21:00 → G1 → HAA (9 jobs, ≈ 8 h; GPU 0 frees ≈ Sep 17 04:00 and can take half) → sim eval → results/analysis/page ≈ Sep 19. Code merges into `main` only in the peer's windows (W1 Sep 15 04:30–20:00; Sep 16 14:00–20:00), each preceded by a message. ICLR deadline 2026-09-24.
183:**Decisions for Yixun (before approval).** (a) Arms D and F (recommended: both; ≈ 5 GPU-hours; they attribute the effect to frame vs channel). (b) Heading source: the axis decision of §4 (default), or a documented DiffRIR loudspeaker orientation supplied as override. (c) GPU 0 smokes co-tenant now under the peer's rules (recommended: yes). (d) H1 margin +0.23 dB (recommended). (e) S1 shared-phase sensitivity pass (recommended: yes, ≈ 1 h). (f) Arm B's k = 0 baseline: reuse exp_05's M-tier evaluation if admissible in time, else evaluate the exp_01 cylindrical checkpoint in exp_06 (≈ 40 min; recommended: yes, it is cheap). Arm A's baseline is exp_04's completed control evaluations.
